o have um over the course  of covid not seen their family  physicians uh as frequently as they they  may have normally would given concerns  with covet uh therefore the acuity of  the illness that  that they're they're facing uh has gone  up and then now they're coming into the  emergency departments so one of the  things that we are doing with with our  budget is working to expand capacity uh  within our hospital systems overall uh  in terms of  we've done that with the with the icu  100 million dollars in specific that and  we've also asked that you know if we  don't need that those those dollars for  the ic  icu to be able to use the resources uh  elsewhere and build capacity within the  system so we're recognizing that this is  an issue  we'll work through that as we we learned  we learned to live with covid and  through uh what the the current uh ba2  wave uh and then continue to build  capacity so that you know we can quite  frankly normalize um and and not saying  it's ever going to be normal but we  shouldn't have to be over a hundred  percent on regular times a year and and  and the only other concept that i would  provide is that you know we're dealing  with covert right now but but also we  you know flu seasons uh we've had to  deal with this in in the past not not as  uh severe  and not the high not as high as levels  but we need to actually invest into our  health care system which we're doing so  that you know we don't have people doing  a high dive to provide services all the  time but this takes time so we have  budgeted for this year and then the next  the next few years to be able to do that  as we recruit and train more staff  thanks minister dan do you have a  follow-up  yes sorry how much  do you feel you know community supports  outside the hospital  should be part of that  expansion that you're that you're  talking about  so when we talk about expansion it's  it's not only within the hospitals per  se so it's not only acute care um it is  also